# Data Pipeline Architecture & Implementation Plan: Multi-Benchmark Traffic Sign Recognition

## Executive Summary & What Has Been Achieved

We have designed and implemented a production-grade, unified PyTorch data pipeline capable of ingesting, preprocessing, augmenting, and batching three major traffic sign classification benchmarks located in `root/data`:

1. **German Traffic Sign Recognition Benchmark (GTSRB)** — 43 classes
2. **Belgium Traffic Sign Classification Benchmark (BelgiumTSC)** — 62 classes
3. **Chinese Traffic Sign Dataset (CTSD)** — 58 classes

The pipeline abstracts dataset-specific nuances (varying folder hierarchies, annotation formats like CSV and semicolon-separated files, image formats including PNG and PPM, and bounding box coordinate conventions) behind a single, consistent PyTorch interface.

